-- Q10733: C Corporations [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 1223(2), when a corporation acquires property with a transferred basis under Section 362 in a Section 351 exchange, it tacks the transferor''s holding period. The corporation includes Torres''s four years plus its own six months, totaling four years and six months.
Wrong (A): This ignores the tacking rule under Section 1223(2), which applies whenever the corporation''s basis is determined by reference to the transferor''s basis.
Wrong (B): There is no minimum one-year requirement that overrides the tacking rule. The actual holding period is calculated by adding the transferor''s period.
Wrong (D): The holding period does not end at the exchange date. The corporation continues to accumulate holding period time after the Section 351 transfer.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10733;

