  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 318(a)(1), a spouse''s stock is attributed to the shareholder. Without a waiver under Section 302(c)(2), Monroe constructively owns the spouse''s 30%, so the interest is not completely terminated. The redemption is treated as a Section 301 dividend distribution.
Wrong (A): Complete termination under Section 302(b)(3) requires elimination of the shareholder''s entire interest, including constructively owned shares. Family attribution must be applied unless affirmatively waived.
Wrong (C): Section 302(b)(1) requires the redemption to not be essentially equivalent to a dividend, but with 30% constructive ownership remaining, the meaningful reduction test is not met.
