UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 707(a)(2)(B) and Treas. Reg. 1.707-3, a contribution followed by a related distribution within two years is presumed to be a disguised sale. Norton is treated as selling the land for $500,000, recognizing $300,000 gain ($500,000 minus $200,000 basis).
Wrong (A): This ignores the disguised sale presumption that applies when a distribution is closely related in time to the contribution under the two-year rule.
Wrong (B): Guaranteed payments under Section 707(c) compensate for services or capital use. A disguised sale is the correct recharacterization here.
Wrong (C): There is no partial sale treatment under the disguised sale rules. The entire transaction is recharacterized as a sale at FMV.$EXPL$
