-- Q10744: Partnerships [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 709(b), organizational expenses up to $5,000 are deductible in the first year (with phase-out above $50,000 total). Since the $4,000 legal fees are under the $5,000 threshold, they are fully deductible. Syndication expenses under Section 709(a) are never deductible or amortizable and must be permanently capitalized.
Wrong (A): This incorrectly treats syndication expenses as amortizable. Only organizational expenses qualify for amortization; syndication costs must be capitalized permanently.
Wrong (B): Syndication expenses cannot be deducted currently. Section 709(a) explicitly prohibits both deduction and amortization of syndication costs.
Wrong (C): While organizational expenses may be currently deductible, syndication expenses are never deductible as ordinary and necessary business expenses.$EXPL$
