-- Q10748: Partnerships [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 704(e)(2), when a partnership interest is acquired by gift and capital is a material income-producing factor, reasonable compensation for the donor''s services must first be allocated. After deducting Harrison''s $200,000 reasonable compensation from $500,000, Riley''s maximum allocation is 40% of the remaining $300,000 = $120,000.
Wrong (A): This ignores the requirement under Section 704(e)(2) to first allocate reasonable compensation for services rendered by the donor partner before computing the donee''s share.
Wrong (B): A donee who receives a capital interest by gift can be a valid partner under Section 704(e)(1) even without performing services, as long as capital is a material income-producing factor.
Wrong (C): The $100,000 partial services allocation has no basis in the statute. Section 704(e)(2) requires deducting full reasonable compensation, not an arbitrary partial amount.$EXPL$
