  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Section 704(d), a partner''s distributive share of loss is deductible only to the extent of outside basis. Keane deducts $35,000 (her full basis), and the excess $15,000 is suspended and carries forward indefinitely until her basis is restored through income allocations, contributions, or additional liabilities.
Wrong (B): A partner''s outside basis cannot go below zero. Losses exceeding basis are suspended, not deducted.
Wrong (C): The excess loss is not permanently disallowed. Section 704(d) suspends the loss indefinitely until basis is restored.
Wrong (D): Keane can deduct up to her $35,000 basis. The limitation caps the deduction at basis, not at zero when the loss exceeds basis.$EXPL$
