-- Q10756: Partnerships [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 721, any contribution of property to a partnership in exchange for a partnership interest is tax-free with no control requirement. This differs from Section 351, which requires transferors to control at least 80% of the corporation immediately after transfer.
Wrong (A): Section 721 does require property rather than services for nonrecognition treatment. A services-for-interest exchange is taxable under Section 83.
Wrong (B): Section 721 does require the contributor to receive a partnership interest in exchange. This is a fundamental requirement of the nonrecognition rule.
Wrong (C): Section 721 applies to contributions to both domestic and foreign partnerships, though foreign partnerships may trigger additional reporting requirements.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10756;

-- Q10757: Partnerships [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 737, when a partner who contributed appreciated property receives a distribution of other property within seven years, gain equals the lesser of (1) FMV of distributed property minus outside basis ($100,000 - $60,000 = $40,000) or (2) net precontribution gain ($90,000). Owen recognizes $40,000.
Wrong (A): Section 737 limits gain to the lesser of the two measures. The full $90,000 precontribution gain is not triggered because the FMV-minus-basis measure is lower.
Wrong (B): The gain is computed under Section 737''s specific formula, not by the appreciation in the distributed property itself.
Wrong (D): Section 737 specifically applies when a contributing partner of appreciated property receives other property within seven years. Distributions of other property can trigger gain.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10757;

