  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 469 and Temp. Reg. 1.469-5T, material participation requires meeting one of seven tests. The most common test requires more than 500 hours, and Dalton''s 450 hours falls short. The 100-hour significant participation test also fails because other individuals participated more.
Wrong (A): The 100-hour test under Temp. Reg. 1.469-5T(a)(3) requires that no other individual participated more than the taxpayer. Two employees each worked 600 hours, exceeding Dalton.
Wrong (B): The facts do not state Dalton is a general partner or manager. Regardless, material participation is determined by hours and the seven regulatory tests.
