-- Q10762: Partnerships [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Sections 754 and 743(b), the election creates a basis adjustment only for the specific transferee at the time of transfer. Abbott receives a $100,000 step-up ($400,000 outside basis minus $300,000 share of inside basis). Briggs is unaffected now, but the ongoing election means any future buyer of his interest would receive a 743(b) adjustment.
Wrong (A): Briggs does not receive an immediate step-down. Section 743(b) adjustments apply only at the time of a transfer, not retroactively to existing partners.
Wrong (B): Briggs does not need to amend prior returns. The Section 754 election is prospective and does not retroactively alter prior years'' tax treatment.
Wrong (D): The Section 754 election applies to the entire partnership, not just to Abbott. Once made, it applies to all future transfers and distributions under Sections 743 and 734.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10762;

