  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 751(c), unrealized receivables include potential Section 1245 recapture. The equipment has $100,000 of accumulated depreciation subject to recapture. Grey''s 25% share equals $25,000 of ordinary income attributable to unrealized receivables upon sale of his interest.
Wrong (A): This calculates Grey''s share of total gain ($140,000 x 25% = $35,000) rather than isolating the Section 1245 depreciation recapture component.
Wrong (B): The difference between FMV and original cost measures gain beyond recapture. Unrealized receivables under Section 751(c) focus on the recapture amount, not total appreciation.
