-- Q10765: Partnerships [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 732(b), in a liquidating distribution the distributee partner''s basis in the distributed property equals the partner''s remaining outside basis. Bishop''s $55,000 outside basis becomes the land''s basis, creating a step-up from the $40,000 inside basis.
Wrong (A): This applies the current distribution rule under Section 732(a)(1), which limits basis to inside basis. In a liquidating distribution, the partner''s outside basis controls.
Wrong (C): Fair market value is not used for basis determination in partnership distributions. Section 732(b) substitutes the partner''s outside basis.
Wrong (D): There is no averaging method in Subchapter K. The basis is determined solely under Section 732(b) using the partner''s outside basis.$EXPL$
